wer follow-ups cannot satisfy the canonical assignment-freshness check.  <!-- lane=code -->\\n<!-- findings:end -->\\n\\n## Code review\\n\\n**F1 requires changes.** The new protocol permits a coordinator to follow up an existing root-created reviewer without another root assignment. However, `local/bin/telemetry.py:562` recognizes assignments only when the message author is the reviewer\\u2019s direct parent. `local/bin/native_review.py:65` then requires that recognized assignment to postdate the review request.\\n\\nAn in-memory regression reproduced the failure: a fresh coordinator assignment and completion retained the previous parent-assignment timestamp, causing `completed_review` to reject the result with `review requires a fresh independently assigned native turn`. A root-authorized prepared record does not resolve this because neither validator consumes that authorization.\\n\\nKeep reviewer reassignment parent-issued until authenticated delegation is implemented and tested. Do not relax the validator to accept arbitrary senders.\\n\\n**Mathematical audit.** No mathematical blocker found. The three combining-polynomial statements remain unchanged and preserve the degree and evaluation conclusions of `eq:combine-lines`. The collision bound explicitly retains nondegeneracy and coefficient-vector inequality. Direct-game estimates remain supplied-witness auxiliaries, not replacements for `lem:qld-4-7`.\\n\\n**Verification.** Three focused Lean checks passed; 14 key declarations depend only on standard axioms. All 26 targeted workflow tests passed. The two remaining `sorry` warnings in `Defs.lean` are unchanged, named normalization obligations. No full rebuild was run; the separately installed `lean-conventions` reference was unavailable.\\n\\nThe prior ledger contained no findings. I used the authoritative patch beyond the truncated attachment and left the checkout unchanged.\\n\",\n  \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIP